  "detokenized": "I have two rule violations to address:\n1. `ts-set-map`: I used `new Set<Outcome>` for TERMINAL_OUTCOMES. Since it's a static lookup table of known values, I should use `Record<Outcome, true>` or `Record<string, true>`.\n2. `ts-no-tiny-functions`: My `isDenormalized` function is a tiny function (one expression). I should inline it.\n\nAlso, I notice I have a structural issue: `canonicalizeArray` is declared twice. Let me rewrite the whole file cleanly, fixing all these issues.\n\nLet me restructure the canonicalization code properly. The issue is that I had a first `canonicalizeArray` declaration, then a second one later. I need to have only one definition.\n\nLet me rewrite the whole file properly.</think>I see two rule violations (`ts-set-map` for the static Set, `ts-no-tiny-functions` for the one-liner `isDenormalized`) and a duplicate function declaration. Let me rewrite the whole file cleanly.<tool_call>write<arg_key>i</arg_key><arg_value>i</arg_key><arg_value>Rewrite tool-loop-guard.ts cleanly with all fixes</arg_value><arg_key>path</arg_key><arg_value>C:/code/poolside-strata/performance/tool-call-investigation/scratch/src/tool-loop-guard.ts</arg_value><arg_key>content</arg_key><arg_value>export const MAX_ADMISSIONS: number = 12;\nexport const MAX_TRANSIENT_FAILURES: number = 2;\nexport type Outcome = \"ok\" | \"no_matches\" | \"transient_error\" | \"permanent_error\" | \"cancelled\";\nexport type DenialReason = \"turn_closed\" | \"invalid_call\" | \"in_flight\" | \"repeat_terminal\" | \"retry_exhausted\" | \"budget_exhausted\";\nexport type Admission = { allowed: true; ticket: string } | { allowed: false; reason: DenialReason };\nexport interface Snapshot {\n  turnId: string | null;\n  revision: number;\n  admissions: number;\n  pending: number;\n  closed: boolean;\n}\n\ntype TicketInfo = {\n  generation: number;\n  tool: string;\n  signature: string;\n  revision: number;\n  completed: boolean;\n};\n\ntype SignatureEntry = {\n  revision: number;\n  pending: boolean;\n  terminal: boolean;\n  transientFailures: number;\n};\n\nconst TERMINAL_OUTCOMES: Record<Outcome, true> = {\n  ok: true,\n  no_matches: true,\n  permanent_error: true,\n  transient_error: false,\n  cancelled: false,\n};\n\n// --- Canonical signature validation/serialization (R07) ---\n\nfunction isPlainObject(value: unknown): value is object {\n  if (value === null) return false;\n  if (typeof value !== \"object\") return false;\n  const proto = Object.getPrototypeOf(value);\n  return proto === Object.prototype || proto === null;\n}\n\n// Validates a value against R07 rules and returns a canonical JSON string.\n// Returns null if the value is invalid. Never invokes getters.\nfunction canonicalize(value: unknown, seen: Set<object>): string | null {\n  if (value === null) return \"null\";\n  if (typeof value === \"boolean\") return value ? \"true\" : \"false\";\n  if (typeof value === \"string\") return JSON.stringify(value);\n  if (typeof value === \"number\") {\n    if (!Number.isFinite(value)) return null;\n    return Object.is(value, -0) ? \"0\" : String(value);\n  }\n  if (typeof value === \"bigint\" || typeof value === \"symbol\" || typeof value === \"function\") return null;\n\n  if (!isPlainObject(value)) return null;\n\n  if (seen.has(value)) return null;\n  seen.add(value);\n  try {\n    if (Array.isArray(value)) return canonicalizeArray(value, seen);\n    return canonicalizeObject(value, seen);\n  } finally {\n    seen.delete(value);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction canonicalizeArray(value: unknown[], seen: Set<object>): string | null {\n  const allOwn = Object.getOwnPropertyNames(value);\n  for (const k of allOwn) {\n    if (k !== \"length\") return null;\n  }\n  let result = \"[\";\n  for (let i = 0; i < value.length; i++) {\n    if (i > 0) result += \",\";\n    const item = canonicalize(value[i], seen);\n    if (item === null) return null;\n    result += item;\n  }\n  result += \"]\";\n  return result;\n}\n\nfunction canonicalizeObject(val